   -p "{\"spec\": {\"requestRollout\": \"<lastCompletedRolloutRequest-value>\"}}"
 ```
 
+{{< note >}}
+
+If you staged the upgrade by updating `environmentdImageRef` before triggering
+the rollout, also revert `environmentdImageRef` to the image of the last
+completed rollout. You can retrieve it from your Materialize CR:
+
+```shell
+kubectl get materialize <instance-name> -n materialize-environment -o jsonpath='{.status.lastCompletedRolloutEnvironmentdImageRef}'
+```
+
+Then, set `environmentdImageRef` back to this value:
+
+```shell
+kubectl patch materialize <instance-name> \
+  -n materialize-environment \
+  --type='merge' \
+  -p "{\"spec\": {\"environmentdImageRef\": \"<lastCompletedRolloutEnvironmentdImageRef-value>\"}}"
+```
+
+If you revert only `requestRollout` and leave `environmentdImageRef` pointing at
+the new version, the Operator keeps the balancerd and console components on the
+image of the last completed rollout, so they stay in sync with the running
+environmentd. However, the spec image remains ahead of what environmentd is
+actually running, so reverting both fields is recommended.
+
+{{< /note >}}
+
